counterfactuals.output:
A dual-pinion electric power steering apparatus comprising:

a rack shaft configured to turn a wheel member;

a steering-wheel pinion configured to mesh with a first rack tooth section formed on the rack shaft and to transmit a steering force from a steering wheel to the rack shaft;

an assist-motor pinion configured to mesh with a second rack tooth section formed on the rack shaft and to transmit an assist force from an electric assist motor to the rack shaft;

a first rack guide disposed opposite the steering-wheel pinion and configured to support the rack shaft at the first rack tooth section; and

a second rack guide disposed opposite the assist-motor pinion and configured to support the rack shaft at the second rack tooth section,

wherein the first rack guide and the second rack guide have different rigidity from each other.
